+# Task 54 D7 — closed dataset acquisition refinement
+
+Status: proposed for independent SPEC/QUALITY review, 2026-11-08. No reader implementation or runtime authority is released by this document. Root fully read the retained-reader integration map and its focused addendum (SHA256 4266520bb4a4237c1e68ee7c373ae7001b14aaa35aaa62cddd0e84dc663ec1a1); its original 30,490-byte prefix is unchanged. Source inspection is fixed at 2da02ab7c861c7d85ff25c4ee5bf67f4d86a6c72. The intervening cleanup commit 2ce43c2 changes no relevant source.
+
+## Problem and intended decision
+
+Schema section 5 bounds external evidence at 8,388,608 bytes per raw file and requires held File/read stamp/immutable bytes for canonical inputs too. The registered Fashion training IDX is 47,040,016 bytes. Existing typed loaders whole-read before shape/hash validation; no pre-read typed byte budget authorizes that file. Applying the report limit to all inputs would strand four declared Fashion profiles (510 family Full rows and 51 Quick projections); omitting those rows would not complete Task 54. Registered MNIST uses 4,800 training and 10,000 test rows at196 features; its largest raw NPY is7,840,128 bytes and does not cause this conflict.
+
+Proposed ruling: define a closed canonical DatasetInput acquisition policy, selected from the actual RegisteredCase and fixed input inventory, before any materialization read/allocation. It requires the exact sizes below in addition to the already-registered content digests, types and shapes. This is an explicit acquisition refinement, not an assertion that existing typed readers already enforce it. It does not raise external report/evidence limits. FileRef lengths describe checked files; callers and artifacts cannot choose an acquisition cap or path.
+
+## Closed raw dataset inventory
+
+Paths are repository-relative identities resolved beneath the actual trusted root; never open an artifact-provided path. A selected case acquires the complete existing dataset inventory required by its resolver, not the union unnecessarily and not a subset chosen to fit memory. The registry, locks, manifests and acquisition policy must agree; mismatch refuses.
+
